/tmp/paper2602.TH19sM/main_edits.tex:710:We generate a similar set of 1000 $3\times 3$ matrices that have entries close to some positive integer $t$, which we choose from a uniform distribution on $[3,100]$. In particular, we use the same lattice distribution sampler as before with $\sigma=2$ centered at $(t,t)^\top$ to generate 3 points inside $\cone((1,0)^\top, (1,2)^\top)$ that form a diagram similar to that of Figure~\ref{fig:graphicexample3}. To obtain the corresponding matrix we evaluate the 3 points at $x,y,$ and $2x-y$.
/tmp/paper2602.TH19sM/main_edits.tex:712:In Figure~\ref{fig:numerics_n}, we plot the average value $x$ of the entries of each matrix versus its factorization time. Red stars indicate matrices of nonnegative integer rank~3, while blue circles indicate rank 2. 
