codex
The paper immediately changes the triage picture: Section 2 reduces every rank-two instance to a \(3\times3\) instance in polynomial time, and Section 3 gives a complete search algorithm. The authors also report an average factorization time of only 0.00812 seconds on their random \(3\times3\) tests. That rules out an honest Track A claim for the paper’s native random distribution; I’m now checking whether a deliberately structured, high-entry Track B family has a large enough measured mechanical-search/compact-insight gap to be meaningful.
