% %one just have to note that if we take $d$ to be the greatest common divisor between all the $2 \times 2$ minors of the matrix $B$, then $d\alpha$ and $d \beta$ must be integer. Just note that the minors of $[b1,b3]$ and $[b2,b3]$ are attained just by multiplying the minors of $B$ by $\beta$ and $\alpha$ respectively. 
