64524:On eight shipping instances, this module's exact implementation of Algorithm 1 succeeded 8/8, as expected, after a mean 6,890,634 candidate splits and 140,276,883 counted exact operations.  The stored final selftest measured 4.95 seconds mean and 6.47 seconds maximum; repeated eight-seed runs produced 4.95–8.02-second means as host load varied.  That is the Track B hardness basis.  The compressed route is to recognize central symmetry: compute the common complementary sum from the centroid, primitive-normalize it, pair complements, gcd-normalize their differences, and halve sum plus/minus difference.  It took 163 operations on the measured shipping instance and at most 165 in preset checks.
