The revised construction now defeats the simple “take coordinate minima/maxima and normalize sum/difference” shortcut on all eight audit seeds. Its intended route remains exact and compact (135 operations at `hard`), while the paper’s bounded-triangle search still has millions of candidates. I’m running the full gate suite next, including 200,000 structure-aware guesses and eight reference-algorithm solves.
