-The G8 key is a strong cheap invariant—absolute determinant multisets, primitive contents, and boundary areas—not a complete canonical form for arbitrary planar configurations.  It is nevertheless invariant under all point reorderings and tested unimodular coordinate changes, and it separated every unrelated test instance.
+G and V pass.  H does not.
 
